{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484188-evoke-the-storm-or-anything-similar","id":1484188,"title":"Evoke the Storm or anything similar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-16T02:11:31-07:00","id":1484188,"title":"Evoke the Storm or anything similar","content":"So, I have one Koldun player in one of my elder games. He is a mighty Koldun, specialized in the Way of Fire. So he wants to summon a powerful fire attack to destroy his nemesis through a ritual. He read the Koldunic Ritual &quot;Evoke the Storm&quot; and wanted to use something similar, but related to his way of fire. Something like a firestorm, like the one we see in Vampire Redemption. But then, the problem is that the Ritual &quot;Evoke the Storm&quot; doesn't have a system, Here's the ritual, from V20 Dark Ages: Tome of Secrets, p. 52:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Evoke the Storm Level Four Rite \u2014 The Transylvanian Kraina \u2014 Attribute: Wits One of the mightiest known kraina rites; Evoke the Storm allows the Cainite to summon foul weather, lightning strikes, and horrendous gales. The koldun using this rite have sunk ships, electrocuted warlords to death in their gleaming armor, and made rivers burst their banks and wash away villages. System: To activate the powers imbued by this rite, the Cainite must stand somewhere elevated and open, where the full horizon can be viewed without obstruction, such as a cliff or grand castle. From this point, the sorcerer can summon forth gales and storms anywhere he can see, stopping just short of hurricanes. The effects of this power are to be determined by the player, with agreement by the Storyteller. This permanent rite is waived if the practitioner is ever awake past the dawn. </div> </div> </div>The problematic part is &quot;The effects of this power are to be determined by the player, with agreement by the Storyteller.&quot; I've been thinking of making it a more localized version of &quot;Jaws of the Dracon&quot;, using the same pool, i.e. Willpower + Occult dices of aggravated damage and make it a higher level ritual, the character has Koldunism 6, so I guess at level 6 it would be reasonable. What do you guys think about it? Do you have any other suggestion? It's a very old game and we want to have fun, so I don't want to let my player down, he nearly lost his character some sessions ago lol. Any feedback is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T03:10:27-07:00","id":1484192,"title":"","content":"Evoke the storm is essentially just the thaumaturgy path &quot;Weather control/Potestas Tempestatum&quot; for kraina users and they roll wits + Occult for it rather than willpower.<br /> <br /> A fire version would be a pretty easy write-up. Take Weather control and re-flavor everything to be heat, drought, desert, or dust. Have your player roll wits + occult, splitting successes between the number of scenes they want it to last and the level of power they want to evoke(1 success equals &quot;weather control&quot; at 1 dot) and have total successes act as both the speed at which the new weather manifests and the attack roll for the 5th dot power(damage dice are just 10 fire damage instead of 10 lightning).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T04:21:05-07:00","id":1484199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484188-evoke-the-storm-or-anything-similar?p=1484192#post1484192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evoke the storm is essentially just the thaumaturgy path &quot;Weather control/Potestas Tempestatum&quot; for kraina users and they roll wits + Occult for it rather than willpower.<br /> <br /> A fire version would be a pretty easy write-up. Take Weather control and re-flavor everything to be heat, drought, desert, or dust. Have your player roll wits + occult, splitting successes between the number of scenes they want it to last and the level of power they want to evoke(1 success equals &quot;weather control&quot; at 1 dot) and have total successes act as both the speed at which the new weather manifests and the attack roll for the 5th dot power(damage dice are just 10 fire damage instead of 10 lightning).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He just came up with the idea of loosely adapting the concept of this seemingly powerful ritual to evoke a really powerful attack with a level 6 ritual against his enemy. For duration, you mean the number of turns it's going to cause the damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T14:11:19-07:00","id":1484233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484188-evoke-the-storm-or-anything-similar?p=1484199#post1484199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He just came up with the idea of loosely adapting the concept of this seemingly powerful ritual to evoke a really powerful attack with a level 6 ritual against his enemy. For duration, you mean the number of turns it's going to cause the damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the normal vanilla game version of evoke the storm, not the new ritual you're creating.<br /> <br /> As for duration, in &quot;Control Weather&quot; the path I'm talking about, you don't do direct damage. The weather gives others a debuff of some kind(for example giving an enemy -2 to all dice-pools and weapon range halved is a level 2 effect) and/or allows the thaumaurge to spend a wp to do direct damage while the weather effect is ongoing(if the thunderstorm is still in the sky, spent a wp to make lighting hit someone specifically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T14:18:14-07:00","id":1484234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484188-evoke-the-storm-or-anything-similar?p=1484233#post1484233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm talking about the normal vanilla game version of evoke the storm, not the new ritual you're creating.<br /> <br /> As for duration, in &quot;Control Weather&quot; the path I'm talking about, you don't do direct damage. The weather gives others a debuff of some kind(for example giving an enemy -2 to all dice-pools and weapon range halved is a level 2 effect) and/or allows the thaumaurge to spend a wp to do direct damage while the weather effect is ongoing(if the thunderstorm is still in the sky, spent a wp to make lighting hit someone specifically).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but then you're talking about the Way of Wind that allows you to direct damage at the cost of 1wp to summon a lightning strike against a foe dealing 10 dice of damage, etc. That's what I mean. The Rego Tempestas version doesn't require a wp point, you just summon the lightning bolt &quot;out of nowhere&quot;, but the difficulty to summon is going to be based on the weather and the damage is again 10 dice of damage. He wants to make a powerful ritual loosely based on the concept of &quot;Evoke the Storm&quot; and &quot;Jaws of the Dracon&quot; against his enemy. I'm more interested in system ideas to use it, as there are very few damaging high level rituals and powers for blood mages, so my idea was using Willpower + Occult as damage dice, as it makes the ritual more impressive in terms of potential damage, because it's not going to be something he can use at will many times etc, he wants to strike at his enemy with full power, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T14:38:30-07:00","id":1484236,"title":"","content":"In any case, thanks for sharing your thoughts to be honest, I'm almost going with my friend's idea of adapting a mage's route to a ritual, just to hasten things and that's why I'm thinking the &quot;Jaws of the Dracon&quot; dice pool is a good call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T16:51:33-07:00","id":1484245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484188-evoke-the-storm-or-anything-similar?p=1484234#post1484234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but then you're talking about the Way of Wind that allows you to direct damage at the cost of 1wp to summon a lightning strike against a foe dealing 10 dice of damage, etc. That's what I mean. The <b>Rego Tempestas version doesn't require a wp point</b>, you just summon the lightning bolt &quot;out of nowhere&quot;, but the difficulty to summon is going to be based on the weather and the damage is again 10 dice of damage. He wants to make a powerful ritual loosely based on the concept of &quot;Evoke the Storm&quot; and &quot;Jaws of the Dracon&quot; against his enemy. I'm more interested in system ideas to use it, as there are very few damaging high level rituals and powers for blood mages, so my idea was using Willpower + Occult as damage dice, as it makes the ritual more impressive in terms of potential damage, because it's not going to be something he can use at will many times etc, he wants to strike at his enemy with full power, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof, I just checked and you're right. I got tremere weather control and modern koldunism mixed up(which is a great way to end up a pile of ash before sunrise...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-16T17:16:32-07:00","id":1484246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484188-evoke-the-storm-or-anything-similar?p=1484245#post1484245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oof, I just checked and you're right. I got tremere weather control and modern koldunism mixed up(which is a great way to end up a pile of ash before sunrise...)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, mixing up Tremere with Tzimisce is akin to real world mixing up Japanese and Chinese in real life, it usually doesn't end well hahaha...<br /> <br /> In any case, I think using Willpower + Occult as damage pool is probably the best idea for this kind of power he wants to evoke. Another possibility would be Manipulation +Occultism x2 as damage (as per The Starvation of Marena).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}